1
00:00:02,503 --> 00:00:05,255
Kevin Malone, you're next. Spit that out.

2
00:00:06,798 --> 00:00:09,468
Spit. Okay, come on. Let's go.

3
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:15,474
You look cute today, Dwight.

4
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:17,601
Thanks, girl.

5
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:23,649
So, yesterday Dwight found half a joint in the parking lot,

6
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:25,943
<i>which is unfortunate, because, as it turns out,</i>

7
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:29,738
<i>Dwight finding drugs is more dangerous than most people using drugs.</i>

8
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:34,159
Let's go over some of these symptoms of marijuana use, shall we?

9
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:37,037
You tell me who this sounds like.

10
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:41,291
Slow moving, inattentive,

11
00:00:42,084 --> 00:00:43,335
dull,

12
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:46,088
constantly snacking,

13
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:49,633
shows a lack of motivation.

14
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,012
Hey.

15
00:00:54,096 --> 00:00:57,975
I like the people I work with, generally, with four exceptions.

16
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,727
But someone committed a crime,

17
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:01,937
and I did not become

18
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:05,482
a Lackawanna County volunteer sheriff's deputy to make friends.

19
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:07,985
And by the way, I haven't.

20
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:45,022
I enjoy the tangy zip of Miracle Whip.

21
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:48,400
Jim does the best impressions.

22
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:51,987
Sometimes he'll look up at me from his desk, and he'll just be someone else.

23
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,739
Like, he'll go...

24
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:02,664
That's supposed to be Phyllis.

25
00:02:02,748 --> 00:02:04,333
I can't do it as good as he can.

26
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:06,918
And the guys are saying, "Chug! Chug! Chug!"

27
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:08,920
But I'm so small and all I had eaten that day

28
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,548
was one of those Auntie Em pretzels from the food court.

29
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:13,717
So I said, "Is it okay if I sip it?"

30
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,053
And they said, "No." But Ryan seemed cool either way...

31
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,262
Stop!

32
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:20,307
This is not "Kelly Kapour's Story Hour."

33
00:02:20,724 --> 00:02:24,519
Illegal drugs were consumed on company property, okay?

34
00:02:24,645 --> 00:02:26,980
Your ass is on the line, mister!

35
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:30,067
My ass is on the line! Now, I'm gonna ask you again,

36
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:33,779
what time did you go home last night?

37
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:35,238
6:00.

38
00:02:42,454 --> 00:02:45,082
I didn't know that you were at a party on Saturday night.

39
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:47,167
I go to a lot of parties.

40
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:49,920
Okay, I'm gonna need to search your car. Give me your keys.

41
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:51,755
I am not giving you my keys.

42
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:53,382
Don't make me do this the hard way.

43
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:55,384
What's the hard way?

44
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:59,388
I go down to the police station on my lunch break. I tell a police officer,

45
00:02:59,471 --> 00:03:02,516
I know several, what I suspect you may have in your car.

46
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:05,435
He requests a hearing from a judge and obtains a search warrant.

47
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:08,230
Once he has said warrant, he will drive over here

48
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:10,816
and make you give him the keys to your car

49
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:13,151
and you will have to obey him.

50
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:14,861
Yeah, let's do it that way.

51
00:03:14,945 --> 00:03:16,905
Dwight! Is he bugging you?

52
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:19,449
Dwight, dude, you gotta take a chill pill, man.

53
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:21,952
It was one joint in the parking lot.

54
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:25,747
You know, you're totally harshing the office mellow.

55
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:27,916
I can't stop this investigation. It is my job.

56
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:29,167
Whoa, you are a volunteer.

57
00:03:29,251 --> 00:03:31,670
I volunteered for this job. And that's not the same.

58
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,046
It is my duty... Volunteer duty.

59
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:35,006
To investigate the crime scene.

60
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:39,094
I have six more interviews to go, and then I will reveal what I know.

61
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:40,303
Narc!

62
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:44,617
If you are attempting to compliment me, then you have done a very good job.

63
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:45,993
I wasn't attempting to compliment you.

64
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,519
Well, you have, because being a narc

65
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,247
is one of the hardest jobs that you can have.

66
00:03:49,271 --> 00:03:50,498
Okay. And I am very proud of being...

67
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:51,666
Why don't you just cool it? Cool it!

68
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:53,775
So... Dwight, please! God!

69
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:57,070
Dude, where's my office? I totally lost it

70
00:03:57,696 --> 00:04:01,116
because I was half-baked, smoking doobies!

71
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:05,203
Doobie Brothers. I was smoking doobies with my brothers.

72
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:07,205
Peace out, Seacrest!

73
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:11,793
Well, your office is behind you. Thanks.

74
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:15,046
Munchies. Who wants some munchies?

75
00:04:15,464 --> 00:04:18,175
I don't think Michael's ever done drugs.

76
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:21,428
I don't know if anyone's ever offered him any.

77
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:24,222
Oscar visited Mexico, when he was five,

78
00:04:24,306 --> 00:04:26,349
to attend his great-grandmother's funeral.

79
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:30,353
What does that mean to a United States law enforcement officer?

80
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,606
He's a potential drug mule.

81
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:36,026
Have you ever taken any illegal drugs? No, I have not.

82
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:39,571
Do you think it's possible that maybe you could have had some drugs

83
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:42,532
in your system without you knowing about it?

84
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:44,951
What are you implying?

85
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:46,578
Have you ever

86
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:51,041
pooped a balloon?

87
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:56,254
Okay, I'm done with this.

88
00:05:03,053 --> 00:05:04,888
He sure left in a hurry.

89
00:05:05,222 --> 00:05:06,473
I don't wanna blow this.

90
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:09,351
<i>This is what all good law enforcement officers dream of,</i>

91
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:12,062
<i>the chance to solve an actual crime.</i>

92
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:15,524
Do you know what this is?

93
00:05:15,607 --> 00:05:17,317
Yes, it's marijuana.

94
00:05:17,526 --> 00:05:19,152
How do you know that?

95
00:05:19,236 --> 00:05:20,403
It's labeled.

96
00:05:22,531 --> 00:05:23,573
Damn it.

97
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:28,745
That is Northern Lights, <i>Cannabis indica.</i>

98
00:05:30,622 --> 00:05:31,665
No.

99
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:33,667
It's marijuana.

100
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:36,115
I'm just saying that you can't be sure that it wasn't you.

101
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,255
That's ridiculous. Of course it wasn't me.

102
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:41,591
Marijuana is a memory loss drug, so maybe you just don't remember.

103
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:42,884
I would remember.

104
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:44,779
Well, how could you if it just erased your memory?

105
00:05:44,803 --> 00:05:45,887
That's not how it works.

106
00:05:45,971 --> 00:05:48,014
Now, how do you know how it works?

107
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:49,975
Knock it off, okay? I'm interviewing you. No!

108
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:52,602
You said I'd be conducting the interview when I walked in here.

109
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:55,438
Now, exactly how much pot did you smoke?

110
00:05:56,898 --> 00:06:00,569
So, Pam told me you do a great Stanley impression. I'd love to hear it.

111
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:03,238
Good.

112
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:08,660
"Why do you keep cc-ing me on things that have nothing to do with me?"

113
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:12,581
Is that supposed to be me?

114
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:15,500
Oh, hey, Stanley. I was just doing an impression.

115
00:06:15,584 --> 00:06:18,003
I do not think that is funny.

116
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:22,173
He does everyone in the office.

117
00:06:22,299 --> 00:06:23,300
Hmm.

118
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:30,640
"I do not think that is funny." "I do not think that is funny."

119
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:32,225
Jinx. Buy me a Coke.

120
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:34,102
No, no! No talking!

121
00:06:37,606 --> 00:06:40,734
Jim is not allowed to talk until after he buys me a Coke.

122
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:44,613
Those are the rules of Jinx and they are unflinchingly rigid.

123
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,580
"Sold out"?

124
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:56,708
That has never happened in the history of Jinx.

125
00:06:57,751 --> 00:06:59,544
Sorry, it's not my problem.

126
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:09,554
I know you're innocent,

127
00:07:09,638 --> 00:07:12,474
but it can't look like I'm treating you any differently.

128
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:14,017
I understand.

129
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,270
Where were you yesterday after work?

130
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,023
Uh-oh, uh-oh.

131
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:24,819
Who's he calling? Ratting somebody out! Narc! Narc!

132
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,447
Kevin. That is so good, Michael.

133
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,449
Remember the narc bit?

134
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:31,451
Okay, I will let them know. Uh-oh.

135
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:33,578
Who's in trouble? Attention, everyone!

136
00:07:33,662 --> 00:07:38,083
Drug testers are coming in a couple of hours to test everyone's urine.

137
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:40,251
What?

138
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:42,063
What are you talking about? Company policy.

139
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:43,672
If drugs are found on the premises,

140
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:47,717
there is automatic drug testing conducted within 24 hours.

141
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:49,219
Is that true, Toby?

142
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,554
When you sign your job application,

143
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:54,432
you agree to comply with random drug testing.

144
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:58,895
<i>Two nights ago, I went to an Alicia Keys concert</i>

145
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:00,748
at the Montage Mountain Performing Arts Center.

146
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:02,649
I had scored these great aisle seats.

147
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:06,319
Anyway, after the opening act, this beautiful girl sits down next to me.

148
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:09,990
And I never get to meet girls with lip rings and she had one.

149
00:08:10,073 --> 00:08:11,950
I don't know exactly how this happened,

150
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:15,120
but one of her friends started passing around some stuff

151
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:16,883
and they said that it was clove cigarettes.

152
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:19,124
And I'm sure that it was clove cigarettes.

153
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:21,501
Everybody in the aisle was doing it.

154
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:25,588
Okay, attention, everyone! The drug testing has been cancelled.

155
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:30,093
Instead, I will be going around to each of you and doing a visual inspection.

156
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:32,762
No, you can't do that. I can do that. It is my office!

157
00:08:32,846 --> 00:08:34,055
No, you cannot.

158
00:08:34,139 --> 00:08:37,892
It has to be official and it has to be urine.

159
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,232
All right.

160
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:45,900
Okay.

161
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:56,161
Kevin, what prescription drugs are you taking besides Rogaine?

162
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:58,663
I'm not taking Rogaine.

163
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,415
Angela, what about you?

164
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,792
I don't take any prescription drugs.

165
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:05,378
You're not on anything?

166
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:09,674
Good.

167
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:16,014
So, the first time we went out to dinner, it was like, whatever, fine.

168
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:20,101
But I was so nervous. So this time, I wanted it to be special.

169
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:21,644
So I bought a new dress!

170
00:09:21,728 --> 00:09:23,748
One of those kinds that's kind of low-cut at the top

171
00:09:23,772 --> 00:09:25,648
to show something. But not everything.

172
00:09:25,732 --> 00:09:27,817
I mean, not everything, Jim. I promise...

173
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:30,070
Hey, guys. What's going on?

174
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,781
We're just having the best conversation.

175
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:36,493
Okay, well, Michael wants to see everyone in the conference room.

176
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,577
But you know what?

177
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:41,247
We have a few minutes, so you guys should definitely finish up your conversation.

178
00:09:41,331 --> 00:09:42,707
Thanks.

179
00:09:44,751 --> 00:09:47,420
So, I was looking so hot...

180
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:50,298
It has come to my attention

181
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:54,803
that some people here think that the use of drugs

182
00:09:55,470 --> 00:09:57,097
is something to laugh about.

183
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:59,349
We don't feel that way. No, not at all.

184
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:01,768
You were the one joking around, calling Dwight a narc.

185
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:03,186
No, no.

186
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:06,189
That was a test. I was testing you.

187
00:10:06,272 --> 00:10:09,901
And you all failed. Miserably.

188
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:14,072
When I said that Dwight was a narc, how many of you defended him?

189
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:16,616
How many of you said, "Hey, you know what? He's right."

190
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:21,121
"What he's doing is protecting this office from the evils of drugs."

191
00:10:21,204 --> 00:10:22,247
Thank you, Michael.

192
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:24,082
I am ridiculously anti-drug.

193
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:28,253
I am so anti-drug that I am above suspicion in any way

194
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:32,298
that involves suspicion or testing of any kind.

195
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:35,093
Drugs ruin lives, people.

196
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:38,304
Drugs destroy careers.

197
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:42,308
Take Cheech and Chong. Everybody knows that Cheech and Chong are funny.

198
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:46,479
But just imagine how funny they would be if they didn't smoke pot.

199
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:49,858
I want everybody to take a look to their left.

200
00:10:50,275 --> 00:10:53,570
Now, I want everybody to take a look to their right.

201
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:58,616
One of those people will be dead from drug use

202
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,869
at some point in their lives.

203
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:04,706
This year more people will use cocaine

204
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:07,167
than will read a book to their children.

205
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:08,626
Where did you get these facts?

206
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:10,879
Are these facts scaring you or are they not?

207
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:12,172
They are not.

208
00:11:12,255 --> 00:11:15,508
Do you think that smoking drugs is cool?

209
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:17,927
Do you think that doing alcohol is cool?

210
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:19,053
No, I don't.

211
00:11:19,137 --> 00:11:23,558
And I have a glass of red wine with dinner about once a week, for the antioxidants.

212
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:25,935
- Yeah, I have the same... - Okay. Enough, enough, enough!

213
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:31,274
I have written down a list of illegal drugs.

214
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:35,236
Take a gander. How many of these are you familiar with?

215
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,363
Hookah is not an illegal drug, Michael.

216
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:38,448
Yes, it is.

217
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:41,201
No, it's not. It's a type of pipe.

218
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:44,913
You can fill it with tobacco, often mixed with fruit or other flavors...

219
00:11:44,996 --> 00:11:46,998
Okay, you know what, Toby?

220
00:11:47,165 --> 00:11:48,416
Pam, could you take this down?

221
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:50,724
In addition to Toby's urine being tested, I

222
00:11:50,736 --> 00:11:52,921
would like to test his blood and his hair.

223
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:54,047
You can't do that.

224
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:58,218
I can test anyone randomly, and I have chosen you randomly.

225
00:11:58,301 --> 00:11:59,677
That's not random. Okay.

226
00:11:59,761 --> 00:12:02,555
Eenie, meenie, minie, moe, is random.

227
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:07,393
Okay, you know what? I'm gonna need a volunteer to select one of these words

228
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:11,314
and tell us of something tragic

229
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:15,360
that happened in either their lives or the lives of a loved one.

230
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:17,612
Yeah, Pam.

231
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:20,531
I know that Jim has an amazing story

232
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:24,285
about a relative of his who got caught up in the world of drugs.

233
00:12:24,369 --> 00:12:25,578
- Really? - Mmm-hmm.

234
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:28,331
Jim, it's okay. You can...

235
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:32,585
This would be a good place to let it out, Jim.

236
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:35,922
These are people you can trust. These are people who care about you.

237
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:37,382
It's okay. Just...

238
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:40,635
We will not judge you. We are here to not judge you.

239
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:42,637
Oh, he's doing it. Okay.

240
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:49,519
It's okay.

241
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:07,912
Okay, are you sure? That looked like it was gonna be good.

242
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:11,291
All right. Okay, well...

243
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:12,875
Wow!

244
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:15,420
He really pulled out the big guns.

245
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:19,132
Fake crying. I did not expect that.

246
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:25,179
The point I'm trying to make with all of this, people,

247
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:29,100
is that I hate drugs. I hate them!

248
00:13:29,726 --> 00:13:31,978
And based upon what I have seen,

249
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:34,897
you all don't quite hate them as much as I do.

250
00:13:35,023 --> 00:13:38,985
So, you are going to have a drug test and I am not.

251
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,654
No, you will be tested. Yes, I will... Will not be.

252
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:45,033
No, you will be. That is the law according to the rules.

